  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA multiprofile scvi is the strongest unimodal direction, with validation accuracy 0.653 and F1 0.628, while the only image result is a weak singleprofile ResNet50 model with accuracy 0.208 and F1 0.172. The key uncertainty is whether the image branch can be made useful by using a stronger image representation before testing fusion. config_013 tests ImageNet ViT-L in the same singleprofile, no-aggregation setting as config_010, so it isolates the effect of image encoder choice. This is the best next use of budget because it is a clean, high-information probe of the image modality: a large improvement would justify subsequent multiprofile and multimodal ViT experiments, while a similarly weak result would suggest image features are currently low-value and we should avoid premature multimodal comparisons that would confound fusion with an unvalidated image branch."
}

